L-134,40,Heraldic,"Newton Flotman Blundeville monument — Constance Gurney + date conflict","St Mary Newton Flotman monument; Blomefield (Henstead hundred), British History Online","Confirm Constance Gurney (dau of William Gurney of West Barsham, G19) m. Ralph/Radulphus Blundeville; resolve the death-date conflict (tomb: Ralph d.1541 aged 74; Visitation: 'ob. 1514' — likely a 1514<->1541 transposition). Dates Constance's father to c.1460-1500.",Y,"Partial 2026-06-15 — printed-pedigree corroboration via FTS (point-8 vector): a published genealogy quoting the VISITATION OF NORFOLK 1563 (Wm Harvey) records 'Anne, daughter of Robert Blundeville of Newton Flotman, by CONSTANCE, daughter of Wm. Gurney of Barsham', and that Anne Blundeville m.(1) John Bastard, son+heir of John Bastard of Bishop's Lynn, (2) Jasper Blake of Wimbotsham (will 17 Jul 1547). So Constance Gurney's husband is named ROBERT Blundeville (vs the tomb's 'Ralph d.1541' — likely father/son or a name variant), confirming Wm Gurney of West Barsham (G19) had a daughter Constance married into Blundeville of Newton Flotman, dating G19 c.1460-1500. FTS ark 3:1:3QHV-B3R2-DK3Z (available online). Open: reconcile Robert vs Ralph + the 1514/1541 date conflict at the primary monument/Visitation.",sources/corpus_supplement/rye-visitacion-norffolk-1891-gurney-selected-pages.md
