L-141,30,G17,"Lovell inheritance — primary IPM corroboration (Margaret Lovell parentage)","Printed Sussex Inquisitions abstract of the IPM of Sir Thomas Lovell KG (d. 25 May 1524, Enfield, s.p.); FTS ark 3:1:3Q9M-CS9T-MS6G-D (collection 'England, Sussex, Legal')","Corroboration (known fact, primary citation upgrade — repo currently cites only Blomefield/Armstrong): the IPM of Sir Thomas Lovell KG names his coheir nieces — Ursula (m. Wm Husey), 'MARGARET GURNEY, wife of Anthony Gurney, esq., aged 26 and more' (=> b. c.1498), Ela (m. John Bylsby), and great-nephew Thomas Fitzlewes — all 'daughters and heirs of Robert Lovell, knt., brother of T.L.' This is a primary-record witness to Margaret Lovell's parentage (dau of Sir Robert Lovell) and the Great Ellingham/Attleborough-Mortimer inheritance that G17 Anthony Gurney brought in. Low priority (fact already established); pull the full printed Sussex Inquisitions entry if the G17/Lovell section is ever upgraded to primary citation. Also incidentally noted this pass: a 1688 Tasburgh court names 'Thomas Gurney of Reyn[a]ther Hall in Norfolk' (ark 3:1:S3HT-DYFQ-NKL) — an unplaced later seated Gurney (?Wreningham/Reymerston; cf. L-28 Tharston), logged not worked.",Y,Opened 2026-06-15 (corroboration),research/people/g17-anthony-gurney-fact-sheet.research.md
