L-144,55,G13,"John Gurney (emigrant) — Tyng Braintree leasehold origin","William Tyng probate (d. 18 Jan 1653, Suffolk Co. MA Probate Liber 1) and earlier Suffolk Deeds / Braintree conveyances of the two Tyng messuages later leased to John Gurney and Gregory Belcher","Date when John Gurney's lease of the Tyng Braintree tenement began, and any earlier events around the property. The leasehold survives only as a March-1661 snapshot (the quadripartite division indenture, done-lead L-103); William Tyng's 1653 probate inventory should show whether John was already the tenant in 1653, and earlier Tyng conveyances could push the tenancy origin back further — bearing on how long John had been settled at Braintree.",Unk,Open,research/people/g13-john-gurney-fact-sheet.research.md
