L-148,40,G13,"Robert Gvrney + Mary, Norwich 1622 — household check","Findmypast England Marriages transcript for Robert Gvrney + Mary, Norwich 1622; parish field + any indexed children","A previously unlogged Norwich Gurney household with a wife named Mary, surfaced in the wildcard marriage sweep. Pull the parish field and check for children — a Norwich Gurney 'Mary' comparator for the emigrant's wife Mary (not a candidate: wrong groom forename, 1622 too late to father the emigrant).",Y,Open,research/people/g13-john-gurney-fact-sheet.research.md
L-149,45,G14,"St Benet Fink baptism register — Francis G14 children reconciliation","St Benet Fink parish register, LMA P69/BEN1/A/001 and /002, baptisms 1619-1638; Harleian Society printed transcript of St Benet Fink registers","Pull to reconcile the Francis G14 + Anne Browning children list across Daniel Gurney (1848), Bernau (1913), and the current G14 fact sheet (Dorothy/Roger agree; 1625-1637 entries diverge). Resolution path for the children-list conflict on the G14 companion.",Part,Open,research/people/g14-francis-gurney-fact-sheet.research.md
L-150,38,G13,"Mary Barton/Burton tradition — provenance test (Ackworth)","Older American Gurney compilations / Rigler 1994 / Google Books — earliest occurrence of the 'colonial John m. Mary Barton/Burton 1636' claim","Identify the earliest source of the Mary Barton/Burton marriage tradition. If it predates modern indexing it is independent evidence pointing at the Ackworth, Yorkshire John Gurnoe x Mary Burton 1636 (raising that row); if it first appears in IGI-era trees it is circular and the Ackworth row stays low. Pairs with continuation-check lead L-23.",Y,Open,research/people/g13-john-gurney-fact-sheet.research.md
L-151,55,G30,"William de Gournay I — Swathings manor within the senior Gournay fee","DG-I Appendix XXI (pp. 122-123) & narrative pp. 207-208 (Vitis Calthorpiana, Harl. MS 970); Farrer HKF vol. 3 corroborates — le Bourguignon/Burgundian Swathings enfeoffment","Reconcile the manorial descent of Swathings: junior-branch lordship (William G30, attested temp. Hen. II by DG-I p.278 and Blomefield) vs. the earlier senior-line enfeoffment of Robert le Bourguignon (DG-I App. XXI; Farrer HKF vol.3). Repo hypotheses: divided-vill multiple manors (hardingham.md) or junior acquisition after le Bourguignon 1204 forfeiture (runhall.md). Trace le Bourguignon descent + Lewis de Gournay tenure.",Part,Open,research/people/g30-william-de-gournay-i-fact-sheet.research.md
